  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "The not sense and the undo sense are two different prefixes in origin and usually translate differently: a negative word for adjectives (unhappy), but a verb meaning undo, open, or take off for verbs (untie, unlock).",
    "grammar": null,
    "culture": null,
    "false_friends": null,
    "pronunciation": "Un- is usually unstressed, but takes strong stress when the speaker contrasts it with the base: not happy, UNhappy. It is usually ʌn, and only rarely reduced to ən."
  },
